{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790010184,"nonce":"REM9rQOA8vX/93rHBHhuukqDZ8U=","title":"Decision: two identities exist for one person; what do we do about it","message":"Found 2026-09-19 while pushing the namespace move, not previously ticketed.\n\nThis store has two identity entities for the same human, same name, same email (Luis Rayas \u003cluisrayas3@gmail.com\u003e):\n\n  7674679  created Sep 14  — what git-bug.identity currently points at\n  a3a2829  created Sep 17  — the one that was already on origin\n\nThey are not cosmetic: 30 issues are authored by the first and 54 by the second. Both are now pushed, because a clone missing either cannot resolve the authors of a third of the tracker.\n\nWhy it matters beyond tidiness: anything keyed on 'who' sees two people. `flow mine` (9a24c8e) returns a third or two thirds of my work depending on which identity it resolves. The weekly report (2c0c256) groups one person into two columns. Jira user mapping (69b7be0) has two local users to map to one account. Assignee filtering has the same problem.\n\nOptions:\n(a) An alias/merge record — one identity declares itself the same person as another, and resolution follows it. Nothing in history is rewritten, which is the only option compatible with content-addressed ops. Needs a place to live (the config entity is the obvious one) and every 'who' query to honour it.\n(b) Teach only the app layer: a local mapping used by queries and reports. Cheaper, does not sync, so everyone repeats it.\n(c) Do nothing and always use one going forward. History stays split forever; the report and flow mine stay wrong for anything older than today.\n\nProbably (a). Upstream's identity has versions and keys but no notion of 'these two are the same person', so this is ours to design.\n\nWorth understanding the cause before choosing: 828c228 (auto-create identity from git config) may have created the second one rather than adopting the first — if so, the adoption path has a bug that will do this to teammates too.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790010184,"nonce":"7JYYl8zhMWjgJBwkatft/Ipqir8=","key":"type","value":"decision"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790010184,"nonce":"3zjYStxK9oOrx/b+4FvJrVKUcP8=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}